## Collections and LINQ

```csharp-norun
int[] arr = [1, 2, 3];
var list = new List<string> { "a" }; list.Add("b"); list.RemoveAt(0);
var dict = new Dictionary<string, int> { ["ada"] = 36 };
dict.TryGetValue("bob", out int age); dict.GetValueOrDefault("bob", -1);
var set = new HashSet<int> { 1, 2 }; set.Add(2);   // false
```

| LINQ | |
|---|---|
| `Where`, `Select`, `SelectMany` | Filter, transform, flatten |
| `OrderBy`, `ThenBy`, `OrderByDescending` | Sort (stable, new sequence) |
| `First`, `FirstOrDefault`, `Single`, `Any`, `All`, `Count` | Pick and test |
| `Sum`, `Average`, `Min`, `Max`, `MinBy`, `MaxBy` | Aggregates |
| `GroupBy`, `CountBy`, `ToDictionary`, `Distinct`, `Take`, `Skip`, `Chunk`, `Zip` | Shape |
| `ToList()`, `ToArray()` | Run now and keep the results |

## Types

```csharp-norun
public class Account(string owner)                 // primary constructor
{
    private decimal _balance;
    public string Owner { get; } = owner;
    public decimal Balance => _balance;
    public required string Iban { get; init; }
    public void Deposit(decimal x) { ArgumentOutOfRangeException.ThrowIfNegative(x); _balance += x; }
    public override string ToString() => $"{Owner}: {_balance:F2}";
}
public record Point(int X, int Y);                  // value equality, with, deconstruction
var moved = p with { X = 5 };
public readonly record struct Money(long Cents, string Currency);
public abstract class Shape { public abstract double Area(); public virtual string Name => "shape"; }
public sealed class Circle(double r) : Shape { public override double Area() => Math.PI * r * r; }
public interface INotifier { void Send(string message); }
public static class Ext { public static bool IsBlank(this string s) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s); }
```

